SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Summary: Clear Mach exception ports inherited from the parent, such as a crash reporter's
Category: system
Kind: fix
Origin: wine-mac-builds
  Note: written for wine-mac-builds (not in Sikarugir). Second Chance does
    the same in the parent before exec today.
Upstream: no (candidate, kept on Second Chance's list for later)
Why: Mach task exception ports are inherited across fork and exec. When
 the program that starts Wine has a task-level crash handler (Sentry,
 KSCrash), faults, bad instructions, breakpoints and software exceptions in
 the Wine process go to it rather than becoming the signals Wine's
 exception handling is built on, and a Windows program hangs at its first
 such exception that goes to the handler. ntdll now clears every task
 exception port (EXC_MASK_ALL, as Second Chance does before starting Wine)
 when it sets up signal handling, except under a debugger (P_TRACED),
 which uses them. It used to clear only bad access, bad instruction and
 arithmetic, and the first int3 still hung under an inherited breakpoint
 port (measured on 10.0 and 11.22).
Programs: none known
Port: to 11.21: same code; called at the start of signal_init_process( TEB * ), which 11.21 already includes <sys/sysctl.h> for.
Status: built in macfixes-11.21-build1; behaviour not yet tested on its own (2026-11-15).
 11.21: 2026-11-26: clears EXC_MASK_ALL instead of three masks; not yet in a build
 11.22: 2026-11-26: clears EXC_MASK_ALL instead of three masks; not yet in a build

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -3093,6 +3093,34 @@ static int libc_addr_cb( struct dl_phdr_info *info, si
     libc_size = size;
     TRACE_(seh)( "found signal trampoline in %s\n", info->dlpi_name);
     return 1;
+}
+#endif
+
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           clear_inherited_exception_ports
+ *
+ * Task exception ports are inherited across fork and exec. If the program
+ * that started Wine set some (a crash reporter such as Sentry or KSCrash,
+ * which take faults, bad instructions, breakpoints and software
+ * exceptions), those Mach exceptions go to that handler instead of becoming
+ * the signals Wine's exception handling depends on, and a Windows program
+ * that relies on its own exception handling hangs. Clear them all, so they
+ * always become signals. Not while a debugger is attached (it receives
+ * exceptions through these ports).
+ */
+static void clear_inherited_exception_ports(void)
+{
+    struct kinfo_proc info;
+    size_t size = sizeof(info);
+    int mib[4] = { CTL_KERN, KERN_PROC, KERN_PROC_PID, getpid() };
+    kern_return_t kr;
+
+    info.kp_proc.p_flag = 0;
+    if (!sysctl( mib, 4, &info, &size, NULL, 0 ) && (info.kp_proc.p_flag & P_TRACED)) return;
+    kr = task_set_exception_ports( mach_task_self(), EXC_MASK_ALL,
+                                   MACH_PORT_NULL, EXCEPTION_DEFAULT, THREAD_STATE_NONE );
+    if (kr != KERN_SUCCESS) WARN_(seh)( "task_set_exception_ports failed: %d\n", kr );
 }
 #endif
 
@@ -3105,6 +3133,10 @@ void signal_init_process( TEB *teb )
     WOW_TEB *wow_teb = get_wow_teb( teb );
     void *ptr;
 
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+    clear_inherited_exception_ports();
+#endif
+
     if (user_shared_data->XState.Size) xstate_size = user_shared_data->XState.Size - sizeof(XSAVE_FORMAT);
     frame_size = offsetof( struct syscall_frame, xstate ) + xstate_size;
     xstate_extended_features = user_shared_data->XState.EnabledFeatures & ~(UINT64)3;
